        "definition": "utterly senseless, foolish, or ridiculous",
        "definitionCN": "毫无头脑、愚蠢或可笑的",
        "example": "It was asinine to drive without a license.",
        "exampleCN": "无证驾驶真是愚蠢至极。",
        "why": "Latin asinus means donkey, an animal proverbially seen as stubborn and witless, so the adjective calls behavior donkey-like in its stupidity.",
